# What the image needs is narrow: the `app` package, `alembic/` + alembic.ini for
# the release migration, and packaging metadata. Everything else is developer- or
# CI-facing.
#
# Excluding a directory here makes it ABSENT AT RUNTIME. A module under app/ that
# reads a file from one of these paths breaks in the container while CI, the
# build, and the deploy all stay green. scripts/check_runtime_entrypoints.py reads
# this file and fails (E3) if anything under app/ references an excluded path, so
# the two cannot drift. Add a directory here only after that guard passes.

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.vscode/
.venv/
.env*
!.env.example
.envrc
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Developer and CI trees — never executed inside the container.
scripts/
tests/
docs/
deploy/
evals/
